WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.060
The internet says he sold 10% of Apple for $800. Wayne calls that false.

00:06.260 --> 00:11.250
So what actually happened? Wayne drafted Apple's partnership agreement, then removed his name 12 days later.

00:12.220 --> 00:17.420
Jobs later sent him $800. Apple was not a corporation, so every partner could be personally liable.

00:18.260 --> 00:23.860
Jobs in Wozniac were young and broke. Wayne was 41 with a house, a car, and money creditors could reach.

00:25.560 --> 00:28.100
The twist? Wayne believed in Apple.

00:28.620 --> 00:31.560
None. It was the right product at the right time.

00:31.800 --> 00:35.300
He left because he expected decades of paperwork instead of building his own inventions.

00:39.200 --> 00:45.480
Lock your verdict, sell or stay. Like, subscribe, and comment now. Wayne says he does not regret leaving Apple.

00:46.280 --> 00:53.780
What did he regret? He sold the original contract for $500. In 2011, it sold for $1.59 million.

00:54.460 --> 00:58.400
That I regret. So was he history's biggest fool or did walking away give him freedom?

